{"artifact_reads":[{"digest_matched":true,"path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-reading-reference/notes/literature-reading-reference-plan.md"}],"concern_count":11,"disposition":"revise","reviewer_id":"qwen","schema_version":2,"summary":"Reviewed the inline plan bytes only (no repository file opened, no probe run), so H1-H22 citations are judged for internal consistency against the rest of the plan rather than against the checkout. The plan is largely coherent: LR1 and LR2 are specified to a testable level under D7 (a) and D2 (b) with R0.1 holding the verify and anchor formats, the lanes in section 9 name one new file per phase plus existing files, and LR3's outline states its dependency on literature-host-interfaces LH1/LH2 and its gate clearly enough (section 3, H17, D9). Two blocking defects: section 2 LR1 prescribes selecting verdicts by a field name (`verdict: \"fail\"`) that the plan's own observed row H2 does not list among the verdict's fields (H2 names `status`), and LR1-C3 checks page field names only against \"the verdict\" although section 2 with H2 and H6 requires the page to name report-level fields (`outcome`, `counts.fail`, exit 1) - as written LR1 would fail its own criterion or have it silently narrowed. Hardening: LR1-C4's deontic and redacted cases have no fixture in section 3; the H2-H4 probe is written as `MODEL POP` so the LR1 baseline cannot be re-run from the plan; `docs/literature/index.md:11`'s \"tied to its passage\" claim is left unreconciled with D2 (b); LR2-C1 has no named verification mechanism; the LR2 home `src/gnd/examples/literature/README.md` carries no criterion while section 7 keeps H9's counterexample; D9's per-stage prompts conflict with H16 and section 3's reading.py limit. Completeness: the writer-conflict sentence and LR1's homes disagree about `index.md`, and D5 shipping LR1/LR2 ahead leaves #226 with no reply until a close that waits on another milestone."}
